{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A psalm of David. I will exalt You</b> — in speech and in faith of the heart." "And he mentioned 'the King' — for He is the King in truth, and this is the foundation of all this psalm." "<b>And I will bless Your name</b> — to add to Your exaltation. Now the meaning is: I will speak, that You are exalted."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 145, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:45.952231702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}